<title>UK: Heseltine 7-4 Conservative favourite.</title>
<headline>Heseltine 7-4 Conservative favourite.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bookmakers on Friday installed outgoing deputy prime minister Michael Heseltine as 7-4 favourite to replace John Major as Conservative party leader.</p>
<p>Former Welsh Secretary William Hague was made second favourite, bookmakers William Hill and Corals said.</p>
<p>William Hill also offered odds of 4-1 that Labour leader Tony Blair would stay in office longer than Margaret Thatcher, prime minister for 11 years. -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7950</p>
